 add('\nResearch observed October 19, 2026. The complete published **2024 Senate** field gives Lisa Blunt Rochester (Democratic) **283,298**, Eric Hansen (Republican) **197,753**, and Michael “Dr. Mike” Katz (Independent Party of Delaware) **19,555**. The pair lead is **85,545 votes**, with **481,051 A+B votes** and **500,606 printed candidate votes**. At those historical weights, a uniform **−8.891468888 share-point** change for A ties the pair; **−8.391468888 share points** yields an illustrative **A+1 pair-margin point**, or **4,810.51 net votes**. The baseline already favors A; no positive improvement is mechanically required. These are conditional arithmetic comparisons, not a 2026 projection. [Official 2024 report](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2024.html), [independent statewide CSV](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2024.csv).')
 add('\nThe November 3, 2026 regular election is **Class II**. The same-seat comparator is November 3, 2020 Coons–Witzke; November 5, 2024 Blunt Rochester–Hansen is the **other, Class I seat**. November 8, 2022 had neither a U.S. Senate nor governor election in Delaware; the actual at-large House contest supplies the midterm comparison. President is always separate. These schedules are verified against the [official archive](https://elections.delaware.gov/elections/election_archive.html), the complete [2022 offices/results](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2022.html), [Class II roster](https://www.senate.gov/senators/Class_II.htm), [Class I roster](https://www.senate.gov/senators/Class_I.htm) and [2026 calendar](https://elections.delaware.gov/public/calendar/pdfs/2026ElectionCalendar.pdf).')
 add('\n**Source presentation and authority.** The archived HTML and linked statewide CSVs are state Department of Elections publications labelled official results. Department county offices administer New Castle, Kent and Sussex; the Superior Court in each county is the board of canvass. This package does not substitute the state web presentation for an independently acquired complete set of signed county certifications. The [office directory](https://elections.delaware.gov/locations.html) and [Title 15 chapter 57](https://delcode.delaware.gov/title15/c057/index.html) distinguish those roles. All source URLs, original bytes or exact shared references, hashes, UTC receipts, HTTP headers, redirects where available, source positions and status qualifications are retained in the [source schema](data/baselines/source/SCHEMA.md), [historical receipts](data/baselines/source/shared-sources.json) and fresh [current](data/baselines/source/current-acquisition.json), [participation](data/baselines/source/additional-acquisition.json), [monthly](data/baselines/source/registration-acquisition.json) and [class-roster receipts](data/baselines/source/support-acquisition.json). Historical shared receipts lack intermediate redirect history; the actual archive href chain was independently recovered. No huge originals are duplicated, truncated or simplified.')
 add('\nThe October 19 [general-election filed list](https://elections.delaware.gov/candidates/candidatelist/genl_fcddt_2026.html) shows **Chris Coons—Democratic—Qualified** and **Michael “Dr. Mike” Katz—Republican—Qualified**. The separate [declared-write-in list](https://elections.delaware.gov/candidates/candidatelist/genl_wcddt_2026.html) shows **William McVay, John Shulli and Travis Jack Stevens**, each Qualified. Their write-in party labels are unprinted here. Complete repeated county-summary/main-list rows remain in [candidate-list evidence](data/baselines/extracted/candidate-lists.json); they are alternative presentations, not additional candidates. Katz’s 2024 independent votes are not relabelled Republican or Democratic. Final ballot order, exhaustive signed/later ballot scope and November vendor candidate/contest IDs remain unverified. The [current results index](https://elections.delaware.gov/results/) still links September 15 primary; its [actual primary report](https://elections.delaware.gov/results/enr/PR2026.html) is retained separately and supplies no November count or identity mapping.')
 add('\n**Statewide denominators.** A and B are the named Democratic and Republican pair in each row. Other retains each actual candidate identity; it is not a Democratic coalition. “Combined” means printed HTML candidates plus separately published named write-ins at the available scope. It excludes unavailable generic-write-in and ballot nonvote quantities. [2020 report/CSV](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2020.html), [2020 CSV](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2020.csv), [2022 report](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2022.html), [2022 CSV](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2022.csv), [2024 report](https://elections.delaware.gov/reports/GE2024.html).')
 add('\n| Context | A | B | Named other | Named total | Separate named WI | Combined published | A pair share % | Pair margin pp |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
