 add('\nThe president/House ranking denominators above are explicitly native **printed-field** totals. Their separate named write-ins are not allocated to native rows. Baseline candidate/raw/position reconciliation matches **all 10,699 rows** and all five complete native descending orders, not just the cutoff. Original-first files and reciprocal immutable snapshots/hashes are retained in [source comparison](data/baselines/peer/reconciliation-v1.json), [rank comparison](data/baselines/peer/ranking-reconciliation.json), [supplement comparison](data/baselines/peer/supplement-reconciliation.json), [stable source manifest](data/baselines/source/stable-extraction-v1.json) and [supplement manifest](data/baselines/source/stable-supplement-v1.json). Peer derivatives are audit inputs only; they supply no baseline counts.')
 add('\n**Participation and registration controls stay source-scoped.** The complete official election-labelled [2020](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/reports/agprpt_2020.txt), [2022](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/reports/agprpt_2022.txt) and [2024](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/reports/agprpt_2024.txt) reports contain 435/519/537 ED identities, respectively. Their 1,631 total rows preserve every county/RD/ED/state and four registration-party group Registered/Voted/% fields, without unrelated age derivatives. Native/RD/county sums reconcile to their own state control. The 2024 participation-only keys **0117, 0222, 0223, 0616** are retained as their actual separate zero-participation source records; no Senate rows are created. In 2022 the participation-only keys are 0228/3117/4117. The 2020 results-only keys are 0218/1314/3117/4117. Source revisions/vintages remain distinct. [Complete totals](data/baselines/extracted/participation-totals.csv), [county controls](data/baselines/county-participation-controls.csv).')
 add('\n| Year | Results header numerator | Results header Registered | Separate participation Voted | Separate participation Registered | Header − participation (Voted / Registered) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
 for r in controls:add(f"| {r['year']} | {r['results_header_reported_votes']:,} | {r['results_header_registered_literal']:,} | {r['participation_voted']:,} | {r['participation_registered']:,} | {r['header_minus_participation_voted']:+,} / {r['header_minus_participation_registered']:+,} |")
 add('\nThese are different original controls with unresolved revision causes, not interchangeable ballots-cast denominators. The results-page label literally says “Registered Votes”; the participation source says Registered/Voted and does not print an exact extract date or active/inactive scope. Registration-party Voted is not candidate choice. Historical blank ballots, undervotes, overvotes, provisional counts outside separately printed fields, generic write-ins and a complete certified ballot-method ledger are unavailable in these products; no header-minus-candidate residual is assigned to any one category. [Source disagreement ledger](data/baselines/source/control-disagreements.json), [official results definitions](https://elections.delaware.gov/results/).')
 add('\nThe separately dated **November1** registration stocks are **2020 RD739,557 / SD738,563; 2022 RD764,765 / SD763,694; 2024 RD790,955 / SD789,403**. Complete 2022/2024 party controls match the RD sums of printed party cells. Native 02-21 Republican and 07-13 Other cells are blank in the 2022/2024 CSVs: those cells and sparse native totals remain null, even though available numeric sums reconcile to printed county/state stocks. These are neither election-day turnout denominators nor current 2026 rolls. The official notice explains why federal-only overseas voters have no state Senate district assignment. All 1,477 Nov1 RD native rows plus distinct SD rows, original party fields, exact dates and county/state controls are retained in [monthly native CSV](data/baselines/extracted/monthly-registration-native.csv), [monthly controls](data/baselines/extracted/monthly-registration-controls.csv), and [original rows](data/baselines/extracted/monthly-registration-original-rows.json). Primary routes: [2020 archive](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/regtotals2020.html), [2022 archive](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/regtotals2022.html), [2024 archive](https://elections.delaware.gov/voter/registrationtotals/regtotals2024.html), [RD/SD notice](https://elections.delaware.gov/candidates/pdfs/RegistrationTotalsPageInformation.pdf).')
 add('\n**Offline conditional live remainder.** The [calculator](data/baselines/calculators.py) keeps counted A/B/each named other fixed and forecasts only an explicitly stated remaining total and its assumed named-other votes. Remaining pair pool is `U=remaining_total−remaining_other`; **final pair denominator** is `countedA+countedB+U`, and **final all-candidate denominator** is `all_counted_candidates+all_remaining_votes`. With counted lead L, final pair-margin target g needs `[U+g×final_pair_denominator−L]/(2U)` A share of the remaining pair votes. Each individual other candidate is checked separately for plurality. No pool, unknown pools/preferences, negative/nonfinite counts, impossible/secured thresholds, clipping and selected-unit-only assumptions remain explicit. Every remaining pool needs a unique source/geography/method key; duplicates are rejected globally.')
 add(f'\nThere are **21 saved synthetic live scenarios**, **6 bounded-shift/selected cases**, nonfinite NaN/±Infinity target fixtures, and **{syn["count"]} substantive assertions**. For counted A40/B60 and 100 remaining pair votes, a final A+1 pair margin requires **61%** of the remainder because the final pair denominator is200. This differs from adding a 0.5-point share cushion on the remainder alone. A synthetic third-candidate case beats both pair candidates even when A beats B; the calculator preserves that outcome. These are arithmetic stress cases, not calibrated probabilities, observed releases, an implemented collector or measured publication cadence. [Inputs](data/baselines/synthetic-inputs.json), [outputs](data/baselines/synthetic-results.json), [bounded cases](data/baselines/synthetic-bounded-cases.json), [invalid targets](data/baselines/synthetic-invalid-numeric-targets.json), [test evidence](data/baselines/synthetic-validation.json).')
 add('\n```sh\npython3 senate/2026/delaware/data/baselines/reproduce.py\npython3 senate/2026/delaware/data/baselines/calculators.py senate/2026/delaware/data/baselines/synthetic-inputs.json\npython3 senate/2026/delaware/data/baselines/validate.py --check-assets\n```')
 add('\nReproduction is offline from complete retained originals and frozen audit snapshots. It builds the report, county/native tables, all-state/every-unit calculations and original-source comparisons, then runs the [validator](data/baselines/validate.py), [validation result](data/baselines/validation.json) and [complete asset audit](data/baselines/asset-manifest.json). All owned assets are strictly below 40,000,000 bytes; no dependency/cache directories are retained. The required coordinator preflight is independently invoked with its writes redirected into these owned paths. Substantive historical extraction, native coverage and deterministic research are complete subject to the explicit source-scope qualifications above. External remaining gates are final official November ballot/feed identities, approved current geometry/crosswalks, complete signed/later legal ballot scope, unavailable historic nonvote controls, measured live cadence, real remaining-pool evidence and calibration. Historical candidate effects, lower preferences and 2026 turnout are not inferred.')
